{% comment %}
  Quick view — the modal shell. Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid, beside the
  cart drawer, and filled client-side by theme.js from /products/<handle>.js when a
  card's eye button ([data-qv-open=handle]) is clicked.

  Shell mirrors the cart drawer: a body attribute (data-qv-open) drives visibility,
  the opener is remembered and refocused on close, Escape and the overlay close it,
  and the rest of the page is made inert while it is open.

  The pharmacy gate is applied twice. The card omits the eye on a restricted product
  in Liquid (see snippets/product-restricted.liquid); the modal also checks the tag
  from the product JSON, exposed here as data-qv-restricted-tag, and shows a link to
  the product page instead of Add To Bag if it is ever handed a restricted handle.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="qv-overlay" data-qv-overlay hidden></div>
<div class="qv-modal" data-qv role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="qv-title"
     data-qv-restricted-tag="{{ settings.restricted_tag | strip | downcase | escape }}" hidden>
  <button type="button" class="cd-x qv-x" data-qv-close aria-label="Close quick view">
    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"></line><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"></line></svg>
  </button>
  <div class="qv-body" data-qv-body></div>
</div>
